`Array.prototype.map()` creates a new array populated with the results of calling a provided function on every element in the calling array. It does not mutate the original array.

```javascript
const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const doubled = numbers.map(num => num * 2);
console.log(doubled); // [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]
```

